to escrow accounts owned by a new offer PDA. Stores the wanted card, the USDC each way, the current fee and an optional expiry. Rejected if the card is not in the verified Collector Crypt collection, if new offers are paused, or if both cards are the same."}]]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"cancel"}]," ",["$","span",null,{"children":"Bidder, or anyone after expiry"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Returns the card, the USDC and the held fee to the bidder, then closes the escrow and offer accounts (rent back to the bidder). No fee."}]]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"accept"}]," ",["$","span",null,{"children":"Owner of the wanted card"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"In one instruction: escrowed card and USDC to the owner, wanted card (and any USDC asked for) to the bidder, the two fees to the treasury, accounts closed. Rejected if the offer expired, if the signer does not hold the wanted card, or if the cards passed are not the ones written in the offer."}]]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"configure"}]," ",["$","span",null,{"children":"Admin key only"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Sets the fee (capped at 10 USDC per side), the treasury, the collection, the $GRADIX waiver and the pause flag. Does not change open offers. Pause blocks new offers only."}]]}]]}],["$","h3",null,{"children":"What is escrowed"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Per offer: the bidder's card (amount 1, in a token account owned by the offer PDA), the USDC the bidder added, and the bidder's fee unless waived. The wanted card never leaves the owner's wallet until they accept. No instruction can send an escrowed asset anywhere except the bidder, the owner who delivers the wanted card in the same instruction, or the treasury for the fixed fee."}]]}]
13:["$","section",null,{"id":"risks","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Risks"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"tx-doc-risks","children":[["$","li",null,{"children":"The program is not audited. A bug could lock or lose escrowed cards or USDC."}],["$","li",null,{"children":"An accepted swap is final. Check both cards before you sign."}],["$","li",null,{"children":"Card values shown are Collector Crypt's insured value, an estimate. They are not a price anyone has agreed to pay."}],["$","li",null,{"children":"The admin key can change the fee for new offers (never above 10 USDC per side), the treasury and the waiver, and can pause new offers. It cannot move escrowed assets."}],["$","li",null,{"children":"Collector Crypt is a third party. A change to its collection, metadata or transfer rule set could block new offers or transfers."}],["$","li",null,{"children":"$$GRADIX is a token on a bonding curve and can lose all its value. Holding it only removes your swap fee."}],["$","li",null,{"children":"Gradix is not affiliated with Collector Crypt or The Pokémon Company. Nothing here is financial advice."}]]}]]}]
14:["$","section",null,{"id":"faq","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"FAQ"}],["$","dl",null,{"className":"tx-doc-faq","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","dt",null,{"children":"Where does the money for the $GRADIX buyback come from?"}],["$","dd",null,{"children":"Only from swap fees: 1 USDC per side on each completed swap. There are no emissions and no outside top-ups. If nobody swaps, nothing is bought. Cancelled and expired offers pay nothing."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","dt",null,{"children":"Who can change the rules after launch?"}],["$","dd",null,{"children":"An admin key sets the fee, the treasury account and the $GRADIX waiver, and can pause new offers. The program caps the fee at 10 USDC per side, and an open offer keeps the fee it was made with. The admin key cannot move escrowed cards or USDC, and a pause never blocks cancel or accept."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","dt",null,{"children":"Do I need to claim anything?"}],["$","dd",null,{"children":"No. On accept, both cards and the USDC land in the two wallets in the same transaction. On cancel or expiry, the card, the USDC and the held fee go straight back to the bidder."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","dt",null,{"children":"What can go wrong?"}],["$","dd",null,{"children":"The program is not audited: a bug could lock or lose escrowed cards or USDC. Card values shown are Collector Crypt's insured value, an estimate, not a price anyone will pay. An accepted swap is final. Collector Crypt is a third party and could change its collection or transfer rules, which could block new offers. $GRADIX can lose all its value."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","dt",null,{"children":"Is there a presale, team allocation or airdrop?"}],["$","dd",null,{"children":"No presale, no team allocation, no airdrop. $GRADIX launches on Pump.fun with the standard 1,000,000,000 supply. The dev buy at launch will be disclosed with its transaction."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","dt",null,{"children":"Is it audited?"}],["$","dd",null,{"children":"No. The program has 20 tests (13 of them attacks that must be refused) run in LiteSVM against the real mainnet Token Metadata and Token Auth Rules programs, Collector Crypt's rule set and two real Collector Crypt cards. That is testing, not an audit. Start with cards you can afford to have stuck."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","dt",null,{"children":"Can I swap a card listed on a marketplace?"}],["$","dd",null,{"children":"Not while it is listed. A listing locks the card, so the escrow cannot take it. Delist it first, then make or accept the offer."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","dt",null,{"children":"What about the Collector Crypt royalty?"}],["$","dd",null,{"children":"The 2% royalty applies to sales. A swap here is two transfers in one transaction, with no sale, so no royalty is charged. Collector Crypt's transfer rule set still runs on every card move."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","dt",null,{"children":"How do I skip the 1 USDC fee?"}],["$","dd",null,{"children":"Hold at least 1,000,000 $GRADIX in the wallet that signs. The bidder is checked when the offer is made, the owner when they accept. The waiver turns on once $GRADIX exists; until then every side pays 1 USDC."}]]}]]}]]}]
